WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
1776, when we founded the light to all nations.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.280
And it's something, really, that an amazing thing

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.840
came out of that date.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.480
It's called the United States of America.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.520
In honor of this momentous anniversary,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.840
I hope that all countries who find inspiration in our example

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:22.240
will join us in renewing our commitment, values,

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.200
and those values, really, that we hold so dear together.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.760
Let us defend free speech and free expression.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.559
Let us protect religious liberty,

00:00:30.559 --> 00:00:34.360
including for the most persecuted religion

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.400
on the planet today.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.720
It's called Christianity.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.680
And let us safeguard our sovereignty

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.880
and cherish qualities that have made each of our nations

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.480
so special, incredible, and extraordinary.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.240
In closing, I just want to repeat

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.080
that immigration and the high cost

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:53.080
of so-called green renewable energy

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.799
is destroying a large part of the free world

00:00:55.799 --> 00:00:58.119
and a large part of our planet.

00:00:58.119 --> 00:01:00.360
Countries that cherish.

